JiraReportBuilder

JiraReportBuilder is responsible for building the final execution model used by the custom eMatch HTML report.
It centralizes the logic that reads execution results, resolves scenario metadata, attaches failure details, reads controlled report steps, and links the correct evidence images to each scenario.

Its main role is to decide between:

• Reading execution data from the report folder
• Building the scenario list from JUnit/XML and fallback data
• Using controlled step notes generated during execution
• Linking the correct evidence image only to the correct failed scenario
• Preparing the final normalized model for the HTML renderer
• Keeping timing, status, errors, steps, and evidence consistent in one place

⸻

🏗️ Position in the architecture

