JiraReportSteps

JiraReportSteps is responsible for creating controlled step entries that appear in the custom eMatch report.
It gives maintainers a simple and safe way to define exactly which step messages must appear in the report without relying on noisy raw execution logs.

Its main role is to decide between:

• Logging only the steps the maintainer explicitly wants to show
• Standardizing the marker used in execution logs
• Making step messages predictable and easy to parse
• Avoiding unrelated internal execution lines in the final report
• Giving maintainers full control of the text shown to users
• Supporting step by step non-Gherkin test projects

⸻

🏗️ Position in the architecture

