ematchReport

ematchReport is the active test listener responsible for collecting execution data during runtime and writing the controlled trace information later consumed by the custom eMatch report.
It is the bridge between live execution and the final HTML report.

Its main role is to decide between:

• Capturing test case start time
• Capturing test case end time
• Writing normalized status information
• Registering controlled report step lines
• Triggering automatic failure evidence capture
• Finalizing per-case context for report generation

⸻

🏗️ Position in the architecture

This class is used automatically by Katalon as the active Test Listener.

It depends on:

• JiraReportSteps controlled step logs
• JiraImagesEvidence screenshot handling
• RunConfiguration report folder
• Katalon TestCaseContext
• JiraReportBuilder, which later reads the data it produces

It should be the only active listener for this custom report flow.

